// Raw Linux system-call harness: the calls only an emitted instruction can make.
//
// Linux-only by construction: a `@FFI.Syscall` is refused at compile time on a
// target that cannot reach the Linux kernel. The engines are the two that put
// the instruction in the program's own image:
//
//   kira test --backend llvm   tests-kik/syscall-harness
//   kira test --backend hybrid tests-kik/syscall-harness
//
// The VM refuses this package before it starts, and not for want of a way into
// the kernel — it asks its host, and tests-kik/syscall-parity-harness is the
// package that does. It refuses because `mount`, `umount2`, `reboot`, `execve`,
// `wait4` and `exit_group` act on the interpreter's own process or on the
// machine running it. See README.md.
//
// main is trivial; the driver synthesized in test mode is the real entry.

import Foundation

@Main
function main() {
    return
}
